PS5 HFR1 / CS2 Nuke / RADV fragment SGPR release A/B/A
2026-11-07, offline 1x, Nuke ~02:38, first-person slot 9, seek tick 10048.
Each run had 10 seconds of warm-up and a 15-second scored window after reseeking.
HFR1 7.2.3-ps5-hfr1, GFX1013, stock MP1, 16 available logical CPUs, split APU
heap, X11 1920x1080 240 Hz, immediate WSI and fullscreen compositor bypass.
All scored Present completions were Flip. Measurements are displayed cadence
using Present UST. P99 is quantized on the 240 Hz MSC grid. 1% low is the
reciprocal of the mean of the slowest ceil(1% * N) completion intervals.
No perf recording, counter build or PM4 dump was active during CS2.

A1 and A2 used system Mesa 26.0.8-1ubuntu0.3. B was a local release built from
the sealed A2-O2-noalias reference with one source unit recompiled. The labels
A1 and A2 below refer to the two stock runs, not the private A2 build name.
Stock-vs-candidate selection is valid for this run. It does not isolate the
patch from every local build difference versus the Ubuntu package.

The release candidate only skips wholly identical direct descriptor SET_SH_REG
packets to fragment user SGPRs in primary GFX1013 graphics command buffers.
It falls back at secondary/DGC and unknown PM4, tracks conditional extents,
and clears shadow state for new buffers and physical IB chunks. An offline
known-answer PM4 diff against the unmodified private A2 build removed exactly
one PS_2 write (c0017600 0000000e 00002000); the tiny IB grew tail NOP padding
and did not change aligned size. Both images passed. The five correctness
checks below ran before CS2. No new kernel entries appeared during B.
The candidate was used only in offline CS2 with -insecure. Stock remained in place.

